d 'POLYCORR': module to compute polychoric, polyserial and Pearson correlations with a joint covariance matrix, bivariate-normality diagnostics and positive-definite repair
d
d      polycorr estimates the correlation between every pair of
d variables in varlist. Each variable is classified as ordinal or  
d  continuous. For two ordinal variables it estimates the
d polychoric correlation, for one ordinal and one continuous
d variable the	  polyserial correlation, and for two continuous
d variables the Pearson correlation. With two categories these
d become the	tetrachoric and biserial correlations.	  Unlike
d earlier implementations, polycorr is an e-class estimation
d command.  e(b) holds all k(k-1)/2 correlations and e(V) their   
d joint asymptotic covariance matrix. The covariance matrix is
d obtained from the influence functions of the two-step estimator,
d so	it allows for the estimated thresholds, means and standard
d deviations. It can be heteroskedasticity robust, cluster robust
d or	design based (Taylor linearization). It is the matrix
d needed to compare or test correlations against each other, and to
d fit	 ordinal structural equation models by weighted least
d squares. 
d
d KW: polychoric correlations
d KW: polyserial correlations
d KW: Pearson correlations
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261030
d
d Author:  Yusuf Toyin Yusuf,  Kwara State University
d Support: email  YUSUF.YUSUF@@KWASU.EDU.NG
d
f polycorr.ado
